0,Mirandese language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirandese_language,"2 weeks ago - Record Mirandese music, with singers including Roberto Leal in his albums Canto da Terra (2007) and Raiç/Raíz (2010). Integrated into the SwiftKey keyboard in 2018, with autocorrect and word suggestions. Participation in the European Language Equality project (2021–2022), which promotes ...",Mirandese,Indo-European
1,"Mirandese Language (MWL) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mwl/,"Mirandese is a stable indigenous language of Portugal. It belongs to the Indo-European language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is taught as a subject of instruction in some schools.",Mirandese,Indo-European
2,An Indo-European Music - ProQuest,https://www.proquest.com/scholarly-journals/indo-european-music/docview/220918127/se-2,"Could he have been thinking of music as well? He posited the proto Indo-European language as a common root, and went on to found the Asiatic Society, a scholastic association that sponsored the translations of so many of the ancient literary treasures of India.",Mirandese,Indo-European
