7,New to Amara: Mirandese and Nhengatu - Amara.org,https://blog.amara.org/2019/08/15/new-to-amara-mirandese-and-nhengatu/,"November 19, 2024 - Two new subtitle languages are now supported on Amara: Mirandese from Portugal and Nhengatu from Brazil. We are happy to share more about these languages! Mirandese (mwl) Mirandese is part of the Indo-European language family and it is spoken in the Northeast population of Portugal.",Mirandese,Indo-European
8,Mirandese | Plurilingual (The Languages Wikia) | Fandom,https://languages.fandom.com/wiki/Mirandese,"in: Languages, Indo-European languages, Italic languages, and 3 more · Romance languages · Western Romance languages · Languages of Europe · Sign In to Save Save Edit · History · Purge · Talk (0) Mirandese is a West Iberian language. Categories · Community content is available under CC-BY-SA unless otherwise noted.",Mirandese,Indo-European
9,Discovering the Mirandese Language: Portugal’s Hidden Linguistic Gem - EnterPortugal.com,https://enterportugal.com/discovering-the-mirandese-language-portugals-hidden-linguistic-gem/,"June 26, 2024 - This status underscores the importance of continued efforts to support and revitalize the language. Initiatives like the creation of a Mirandese Wikipedia (Biquipédia) and recordings of Mirandese music by artists like Roberto Leal are crucial to these preservation efforts.",Mirandese,Indo-European
